{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/core_user/myprofile_node

    One profile node on its own.

    Only for the standalone render_node() path, which exists because it is a public method of
    the renderer being replaced and anything already calling it must keep getting markup back.
    The category template does NOT include this one: a fact belongs inside its card's single
    definition list, so sharing a partial here would emit one list per fact. The duplication is
    the cheaper of the two mistakes, and it also keeps this file valid HTML when the Mustache
    lint renders it in isolation.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * isfact - True when the node carries content and is rendered as a label and value pair.
    * name - The node name.
    * title - The node label.
    * hasurl - Whether the label links somewhere.
    * url - The link target.
    * content - Pre-built HTML for the value.
    * hasicon - Whether there is an icon.
    * iconhtml - Pre-built HTML for the icon.
    * classes - Extra CSS classes.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "isfact": true,
        "name": "email",
        "title": "Endereco de email",
        "hasurl": false,
        "url": "",
        "content": "aluno@example.org",
        "hasicon": false,
        "iconhtml": "",
        "classes": ""
    }
}}
{{#isfact}}
    <dl class="dimensions-profile-facts">
        <div class="dimensions-profile-fact {{classes}}">
            <dt class="dimensions-profile-fact-label">{{#hasurl}}<a href="{{url}}">{{{title}}}</a>{{/hasurl}}{{^hasurl}}{{{title}}}{{/hasurl}}{{#hasicon}} {{{iconhtml}}}{{/hasicon}}</dt>
            <dd class="dimensions-profile-fact-value">{{{content}}}</dd>
        </div>
    </dl>
{{/isfact}}
{{^isfact}}
    <div class="dimensions-profile-action {{classes}}">{{#hasurl}}<a href="{{url}}">{{{title}}}</a>{{/hasurl}}{{^hasurl}}<span>{{{title}}}</span>{{/hasurl}}{{#hasicon}} {{{iconhtml}}}{{/hasicon}}</div>
{{/isfact}}
